{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"THE way to create a control (add_control is retired). Builds the record with the platform's exact internal shape and registers it in the library's controls index, so patch_control_facet / read_control_facet / delete_control work on it immediately. A new control is ADMIN-ONLY: readers [] and no groups label - open it afterwards, deliberately, with set_groups. JOURNALED: the first entry of the new control's patch journal (facet \"control\", op \"create\", new = the record data). Refuses an existing control of the same name; a phantom (name in the index, record missing) is healed under its indexed id (healed:true). An empty author defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous. Use this instead of hand-writing data-folder records (which corrupts the index). Returns FLAT {status, id, name, lib, created, healed, patch_id | journal_warning}.","groups":"admin","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::unique_session_id::unique_session_id;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"desc":"Library that will own the new control.","name":"lib","type":"String"},{"desc":"Human-facing control name (unique within the library); this is what data-control='lib:name:{}' resolves and what other dev.code commands take as `ctl`.","name":"name","type":"String"},{"desc":"Description of the control; discoverable via list_controls / set_control_meta. May be empty.","name":"desc","type":"String"},{"desc":"Who is creating the control, recorded on the journal entry. Empty defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous.","name":"author","type":"String"},{"desc":"Request metadata filled in by the framework; pass an empty string from tools.","name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"isnhix1a108282fe6n3c","readers":["admin"],"time":1795107714156,"username":"system","writers":[]}